reality:
Before each subcontract, the contractor must:
- check the sub's REA registration, its permanent-staff quota and its level in the chain;
- record it in the on-site Libro de Subcontratación;
- get approval for, and notify, any exceptional extra level.
If any of this goes wrong, the contractor becomes jointly liable for the sub's wage and Social Security debts.

Owners and gestorías must track a growing menu of entitlements that courts keep reinterpreting:
- birth leave of 19 weeks, including 2 weeks usable until the child turns 8;
- a 5-day care leave per event with no annual cap;
- force-majeure hours;
- a 4-day climate leave;
- leave counted on the actual shift length.

Firms and gestorías must plan for rules that are announced, delayed, struck down or reinterpreted:
- 37.5 hours, rejected;
- digital registro, postponed;
- pay transparency, overdue;
- RD 723/2026, four years late then effective in 20 days;
- SMI, retroactive;
- the anti-absorption decree-law, pending.
The 29-N election adds a new layer of uncertainty.

